    "created_at": "2016-05-10T15:16:59Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-10T15:16:59Z",
    "body": "This is intentional. A \"valid email address\" for the `<input type=\"email\">` control is not \"a valid email address\" per traditional definitions. Instead, that regexp is meant to match the above ABNF. Please see the paragraph stating \"This requirement is a willful violation of RFC 5322\".\n\nOr are you saying that the ABNF and the regexp don't match? As far as I can tell the ABNF allows `asdf@a` and `.a..@a`, so they are correctly matching.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
