    "created_at": "2016-05-10T17:49:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-10T17:49:36Z",
    "body": "Well, it depends. In the end, the set of email addresses that different email servers accept widely varies, and doesn't match RFC 5322 either in many cases. The idea is that we should do the minimal validation that won't exclude email addresses that someone might use. You can always impose further restrictions with the `pattern` attribute, if you are sure that all your users are using mail servers that follow stricter rules (e.g. if you are writing an intranet page).\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
