    "created_at": "2016-05-10T17:58:59Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-10T17:59:43Z",
    "body": "You are right for some cases, like for an intranet. There could be an email address like `name@local` or something like that, but I assume that in most cases addresses like `name.@a.b` or `.@a.b` should be rejected, since (probably) no server could answer. (At least not yet.)\n",
