    "created_at": "2025-07-28T14:58:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-07-28T14:58:18Z",
    "body": "For the record, back in 2016 when this ticket was opened, `mailto:abuse@ai` was a real email address that you could really email.\n(Anguilla removed their top-level MX record a few years ago, around the time that bitcoin grifters pivoted to generative AI.)\nHere's a quick-and-dirty search for top-level (no \".\") mail servers today:\n\n``` bash\n$ xargs -d\\\\n --arg-file=<(curl -s https://data.iana.org/TLD/tlds-alpha-by-domain.txt | sed -e 1d -e s/$/./) -- resolvectl query --type=mx -- 2>/dev/null | grep -Fw 'IN MX'\nCF IN MX 0 mail.intnet.CF\nGP IN MX 10 ns1.nic.GP\nGT IN MX 10 aspmx.l.google.com\nGT IN MX 30 aspmx5.googlemail.com\nGT IN MX 30 aspmx2.googlemail.com\nGT IN MX 20 alt1.aspmx.l.google.com\nGT IN MX 30 aspmx4.googlemail.com\nGT IN MX 20 alt2.aspmx.l.google.com\nHR IN MX 5 alpha.carnet.HR\nKM IN MX 100 mail1.comorestelecom.KM\nMQ IN MX 10 mx1-mq.mediaserv.net\nMR IN MX 5 mail.nic.MR\nTT IN MX 1 ASPMX.L.GOOGLE.COM\nTT IN MX 10 ALT1.ASPMX.L.GOOGLE.COM\nUA IN MX 10 mr.kolo.net\nWS IN MX 10 mail.worldsite.WS\nXN--MGBAH1A3HJKRD IN MX 5 mail.nic.mr\nXN--NGBRX IN MX 10 your-dns-needs-immediate-attention.XN--NGBRX\n```",
    "author_association": "NONE",
